Course description
This course introduces the benefits of using the Case Validation Tool (CVT), demonstrates how to navigate the CVT and encourages its use as a quality assurance tool. 
Course details
•	Duration: 30 minutes
•	Proficiency level: Foundation
•	Audience: All Staff
•	Prerequisites: None, however you will have to have a good working knowledge of the use of Siebel Case Management prior to undertaking this course. 
Learning outcomes
At the end of this course, you will be able to:
•	Recognise the different views within the CVT.
•	Generate reports in the CVT to support Siebel case management work.
•	Analyse how the CVT improves case work outcomes.
•	Explain improvement indicators, suppressions and quality elements.
•	Locate additional supporting information on SharePoint.
 
1. What is the CVT
The CVT is a web application which uses data entered in Siebel and applies tests to this data. 
These tests are based on current enterprise or group practices, procedures and processes in place within your Group. For example, the tests which apply in the Client Engagement Group are based on Group level practices, procedures and processes for Client Engagement (3.4) work and Interpretative Assistance (2.5) work.
Benefits of the CVT
The benefits of the CVT include:
•	Supporting front line staff in 'near to real time' quality management throughout the duration of a case being actioned in Siebel case management.
•	Reducing the time it takes for a team leader to undertake review of the data and information entered into a Siebel case.
•	Reducing the number of cases needing to be reopened to fix data entry errors.
•	Reducing the time taken to correct errors.
How to access the CVT
Ensure you have the following SAP System Access Roles (SARs) against your position number to access the tool:
