Business activity / industry

Develop an understanding of the taxpayer's business with a focus on understanding the actual business activities undertaken and not on its tax impacts.

Identifying the ANZSIC code, the tax return description and undertaking internet searches is a starting point for this analysis to more accurately identify the industry the entity is operating in.

The analysis should consider the following, dependant on the size and complexity of the entity:

what the taxpayer owns
what they sell, who do they sell it to, how do they make it
how are they structured, entity ownership
what are the goals of the owners?
what industry or industries are they operating in
what are the conditions in those industries; has there been any key changes in regulatory and other laws that impact on the business?
who are their key competitors?
how is the business performing and what are the taxpayer's future goals?

