This ratio should be used as a profiling tool to pinpoint seasonal or one-off event that affect the refund status of the entity. This information can then be used to predict any risks associated with BAS refunds.




Net Cash Flow (G1-G11-8A+8B-W1+W2)

	

To determine the profitability of an entity over the quarter.

	

Variation in net cash flow will indicate the general profitability of the entity over time. This should assist in profiling and predicting possible compliance risks.

	

The net cash flow of a profitable entity is positive over time.

If the net cash flow for a period is negative, then the entity is estimated to have paid out more for acquisitions and tax than it has made from supplies and refunds for the quarter. This statistic should be used as a profiling tool to pinpoint seasonal or one-off event that affects the profitability of the company.

This information can then be used to predict any risks associated with low profitability.

