Lifestyle

SB Personal Living Expenses questionnaire and completion instructions.

Examining a taxpayer's lifestyle aims to identify the PLEs of the family unit associated with the client. You are looking at how they fund the family living expenses, their private assets and if there are any discrepancies in the adjusted income available to support the client's lifestyle.

Go to ECP Client tab > Unexplained Wealth Summary > drill-down link. The unexplained wealth model seeks to identify households that have high lifestyle costs compared to reported taxable income (referred to as lifestyle testing).

Lifestyle testing

Lifestyle testing is based on 2 calculations:

Adjusted net income for the review period (that is, 3 years' worth)

Lifestyle cost for the review period.

Figures are an estimate. Lifestyle cost calculations aim to be as accurate as possible based on available data. However, the calculations should be exercised with caution as the Lifestyle Model incorporates asset holdings and seeks to establish lifestyle costs associated with the assets.

In addition, the model will provide:

a better understanding of the omitted income risk population.

a systematic way of detecting and treating the omitted income risk

a method of risk rating cases from highest to lowest risk using estimated income surplus/deficit.

Lifestyle model

The unexplained wealth model will utilise (but not be limited to) the following inputs:

Data available on ATO systems such as tax returns spouse (or partner) data

Property data

Shares data

Luxury motor vehicle

Motor vehicle registrations

AUSTRAC data

Capital gains

Employment termination payment (ETP)

Superannuation contributions

Family Tax Benefit (FTB) payments

Interest principal variation

Rental borrowing reduction

Household size

Outstanding tax return

Poverty line

Base population

The ATO data holdings organises taxpayers into sub-segments or markets depending on turnover of business or personal income as reported by that taxpayer.

The base population for the Unexplained Wealth Model comprises all individual taxpayers with an active role (regardless of market segment).

Identifying households

The Unexplained Wealth Model identifies households and their estimated lifestyle costs; the output and analysis are based at the individual level.

Review period

Review each identified household for the last 4 completed financial years. These 4 years are referred as the review period. At the completion of the lodgment program for the latest due tax return, the periods will be moved forward to the next financial year.

Establish the individual's adjusted net income and lifestyle costs and use these results in calculating an estimate of the individual's income surplus or deficit. Where a deficit is shown the lifestyle funding risk may exist.

