The approximate calculations by ICP do not take into account public holidays or weekends. It is our practice to add 4 business days to the notice of assessment (NoA) Effective date to more accurately reflect when the NOA was received by the taxpayer.

Note: 

The lodgment of an original assessment for a taxpayer will not always result in an NOA being issued to the taxpayer.
For full self-assessment taxpayers, an assessment is deemed to be made when the form is lodged, i.e. received date of the form in ICP.

There is a known issue with some credit assessments where the NOA Effective date and Date on the NOA is incorrect. In these situations, the Refund Processed date will be later than the Refund Effective date. To determine the period of review, 4 business days should be added to the Refund Processed date and not the NOA Effective date. This will more accurately reflect when the NOA was received by the taxpayer.

