Repayment of assessable income

The relevant legislation is Section 59-30 of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 (ITAA 1997).

An amount a taxpayer receives is not assessable income for an income year if the taxpayer:

must repay the amount, which is repaid in a later income year and 
cannot deduct the repayment in any income year. 

The taxpayer can seek an amendment for the year in which the income was originally included to reduce the amount of their assessable income.

