Recalculating losses carried forward

A tax loss can be recalculated for income years where the period of review has expired. Any remaining tax loss is available to be carried forward to the 'in time' later income years. If the taxpayer has lodged a Losses Schedule with their out of time amendment, the schedule must be keyed, as schedules are not subject to period of review.

Amend only those years nominated by the taxpayer in the amendment request.

Advice

This advice is based on the view that the raising of an assessment for a particular year requires, independently of anything that has occurred in relation to any other year's assessment, a proper application of every provision of the legislation which affects the determination of the amounts of taxable income and tax payable for that year.

The principle to be followed is that the deduction in respect of a prior year's loss is available if:

such a loss has been incurred, and
it remains unrecouped.

The deduction is available in the 'amendable' years despite the earlier year's assessment not being able to be amended. As recalculated, any remaining tax loss from the earlier years is available to be carried forward to later income years. The fact that a subsequent intervening income year has been assessed on a taxable income does not change the outcome of whether or not that assessment is out of time for amendment – see subsection 36-15
