Primary production and special professional averaging

There is no barrier against the use of the correct amount of taxable income (for example, assessable income less allowable deductions) for the year concerned in calculating the average income of a primary producer or special professional for a later year.

Earlier years which are out of time for amendment, can be recalculated and the revised taxable income used in calculating PP averaging or special professionals above average income (SPAAI) for later amendable years.

Note: Amend only those years nominated by the taxpayer in the amendment request.

Where the taxpayer has requested amendments to several years up to and including the current year lodged/issued, then apply the Period of Review as normal and apply the averaging to all applicable years.

Where the taxpayer requested an amendment for a year/s that is OOT and no subsequent years are mentioned, then the PP averaging and SPAAI provisions are not updated on later issued assessments.

