Look-through earnout right

Financial benefits under a look-through earnout right can be provided or received up to 5 years after the end of the income year in which the CGT event occurred. In some cases, the period of review may have passed before the taxpayer has provided or received the financial benefit requiring the amendment.

Accordingly, the period of review for all entities’ tax-related liabilities affected by a look-through earnout right, is the later of:

the period of review that would normally apply, and
4 years after the end of the income year in which the last possible financial benefit could be received or provided under the look-through earnout right.

If the taxpayer is stating the amendment relates to a look-through earnout right:

the applicable period of review is 4 years after end of the income year of the last possible financial benefit
the taxpayer needs to clearly state what date the last possible financial benefit occurred. For example, taxpayer states the last possible financial benefit occurred 22 September 2022. This is in the 2023 financial year, therefore the period of review ends 30 June 2027.

This applies only to labels relating to the look-through earnout right. If the taxpayer is amending other labels for other reasons, normal period of review rules apply. The amendment may be:

partially in time, and
partially out of time.
