System searches
ATO Matching System (ATOMS)

ATOMS provides information about payment summaries for payers and payees and is located in Compliance Online Enquiry and Amendment System (COEAS).

To review the payee details and payer reported information refer to the Data matching - income checks in COEAS (ATOMS) and STP
Opens in a new window
 instructions.  Note: From 1 July 2019, all employers are required to report this type of information through Single Touch Payroll 
Opens in a new window
(STP). STP is accessible via ICP.

Australian Business Register

The Australian Business Register (ABR) stores details about businesses and organisations when they register for an Australian business number (ABN).

Australian Business Research

Australian Business Research is an online database containing Australian and international company credit, financial and intelligence resources. It also includes land titles, business names, Australian stock data, bankruptcy, credit, due diligence and property equity reports.

This database is accessible via Equifax IQ Connect. Refer to the Information Hub
Opens in a new window
 for further information.

AUSTRAC

The Australian Transaction Reports and Analysis Centre (AUSTRAC) is a separate government agency to the ATO and administers and oversees the provisions of the Financial Transaction Reports (FTR) Act 1988. It also maintains AUSTRAC database
Opens in a new window
 for the reports of suspect transactions, significant cash transactions, international funds transfer instructions and other transactions received from cash dealers. Refer to the ATO AUSTRAC SharePoint page
Opens in a new window
 for further information.

Australian Securities & Investments Commission 

You may check the current registration status of a company via the ASIC website
Opens in a new window
. 

Mirrored Australian Securities Commission On Time (MASCOT
Opens in a new window
) is the ASIC database which records the details of an entity's legal requirements under the Corporations Law.

It contains all Australian Company Numbers (ACN), Australian Registered Body Numbers (ARBN) and Australian Registered Scheme Numbers (ARSN) issued by ASIC. The MASCOT database is used in the identification of companies and directors interests, in the formulation of a group structure and the identification of changes in shareholdings for private companies. It is also used to check the solvency status of an entity. Refer to MASCOT - information access and fees
Opens in a new window
.

Enterprise Client Profile (ECP)

Enterprise Client Profile (ECP)
Opens in a new window
 is an effective profiling tool. It allows to easily and quickly view the key available information to start understanding the taxpayer's circumstances.

Recommended ECP gadgets to identify Debt and Lodgment information

Lodgment Dashboard provides insight into the taxpayers' lodgment status and history.

Lodgment
	Information related to the taxpayers's next, last, and overdue lodgments for Income Tax account. Additional drill down links:
ITR Lodgment Status History
Lodgments all

