Displays a count and dollar value of debt write-off transactions that exist for the taxpayer.


Financial Resilience Insights - summary view	

Financial Resilience Insights (FRI) provides a holistic view of a taxpayer's financial resilience to better tailor taxpayer interactions.

IBISWorld

IBISWorld 
Opens in a new window
is a resource centre for analysts and researchers, providing information on companies, industries and economies. The information is valuable when evaluating risk, in assessing industry norms, in forecasting trends and in researching taxpayer links. The information is updated each month.

Instalment Processing System (IPS)

IPS issues activity statements to taxpayers, and processes original and revised activity statements lodged by taxpayers. IPS is also used to processes ATO original and revised activity statements as a result of compliance action and posts the amounts to Integrated Core Processing (ICP). Refer to the Activity statement processing manual
Opens in a new window
.

Integrated Core Processing (ICP)

ICP is our processing system for registrations, forms (lodgments and payments) and accounting transactions for taxpayers, regardless of the type of tax product. ICP enables a whole-of-client view of all transactions.

ICP complements the Siebel Client Relationship Management system and works in conjunction with both case management and work management components in Siebel.

For further guidance on ICP refer to ICP issues and support
Opens in a new window
 and Compliance overview of ICP
Opens in a new window
.

Mainframe

Mainframe applications can be accessed via Mainframe Host Access for Applications
Opens in a new window
 once access has been granted through IT Service Connect. It can also be launched from Siebel using the AIS button on the Consolidated Client View. Refer to the Mainframe training package
Opens in a new window
 for further information.

Systems include:

ATO Integrated System (AIS) - is a legacy mainframe application. 
National Taxpayer system (NTS) - maintains taxpayer history records including lodgment, assessment, amendment, cancellation and accounting history.
Electronic Funds Transfer (EFT) - legacy system provides EFT details, bank usage information, TFN declarations and reports on payer/payee. Information is available on ICP. Refer to FIA - overview, eligibility and guidance page
Opens in a new window
 for further information.
Transaction Searching Facility (TSF) - applies the same data access restrictions as AIS does, however it conducts searches on a 10-year period. Searches on the recent 3 years will return a response within a few minutes. The other 7 years require overnight processing. You can submit a search using any of: TFN, ABN, name and date of birth, name and full or partial postcode, address including full or partial postcode.
For access, ask your Resource Access Control Facility (RACF) administrator to connect you to the mainframe RACF group #TEDI??? (the question marks represent your branch office acronym/code).
Real Property (RP) data

A property and a title search are two distinctly separate searches commonly incorrectly grouped together as one request. The statutory function of registering ownership of land and property is the responsibility of each state or territory. These departments are named differently in each state and territory.

A property search is to look for property belonging to people. This search is accessed from a property database system on a given name or address and can list properties owned by those contact details.

A title search is usually requested when hard copies of documents are required. These documents could be a certificate of title, transfer or mortgage documents. Note: This search may incur a fee.

Searches can be completed online to the appropriate authority where that facility is available or by requesting the information from the appropriate state body.

Check with your team leader for guidance. Refer to Guide to the RP Data Professional platform
Opens in a new window
.

Residential tenancies authority database (or equivalent)

Where the residential tenancies authority is holding a bond for a taxpayer, they may provide either a residential or forwarding address for the taxpayer. This information can normally be accessed through the internet. There may be a cost associated with accessing this information. The information may also be available through Tactical Information Gathering & Evidence Resource (TIGER)
Opens in a new window
.

Check with your team leader for guidance.

