• Suspect Transaction reports (SUSTR)
• Suspicious Matter Report (SMR)
- Teller/staff form a suspicion on a customer
Glossary of Terms
AUSTRAC The Australian Transaction Reports and Analysis Centre (AUSTRAC) is part of the Attorney General’s 
Office and they oversee the administration, operation, and compliance with the Financial Transaction 
Reports (FTR) Act 1988 and the Anti-Money Laundering and Counter Terrorism Financing (AML/CTF) 
Act 2006. The FTR and AML/CTF Acts are an initiative to assist the Tax Office and Federal and State law 
enforcement and other revenue agencies in the detection of tax evasion, criminal activity including 
offences against Australia's corporate laws, money laundering from drug trafficking, organised crime, 
and monies used for terrorism.
AUSTRAC This is the AUSTRAC database on which users conduct searches
Workbench
CBM-MI Cross Border Movement – Monetary Instrument (combined reporting of former Cross Border 
Movement Physical Currency and Bearer Negotiable instrument reports). Carrying and sending 
monetary instruments (MI) across international borders is an identified money laundering technique. 
MIs include physical currency, travelers cheques, cheques, money orders, promissory notes or other 
bearer negotiable instruments. 
IFTI-DRA International Funds Transfer Instruction Report - Designated Remittance Arrangement. This is an 
instruction for the transfer of funds into or out of Australia electronically or by telegraph which is 
completed by a remittance service provider. Reported under the AML/CTF Act.
IFTI-E International Funds Transfer Instruction Report - Electronic. This is an instruction for the transfer of 
funds into or out of Australia electronically or by telegraph. Reported under the AML/CTF Act.
SMR Suspicious Matter Report. Reported by reporting entities when they form a suspicion (at any time 
when dealing with a customer) on a matter they suspect may be related to an offence against any 
Commonwealth, state or territory law, tax evasion, or the proceeds of crime.
SOLTR Solicitor Significant Cash Transaction Report. This is a report that solicitors submit in respect of a cash 
transaction involving $10,000 or more.
Structuring Reducing the amount of a transaction otherwise reportable to AUSTRAC so as to avoid the reporting 
of the transaction eg making 2 deposits of $5,000 in cash.
SUSTR Suspect Transaction Report. This is a report that cash dealers submit when they believe a suspicious 
financial transaction has occurred or been attempted.
TRNFR-SW IFTI Transfer Report. A particular type of IFTI where the both the 'Sending Institution' (origin of the 
funds) and the 'Account with institution' (where the funds end up) reside outside Australia.
TTR-FBS Threshold Transaction Report. A report of a transfer of physical currency or e-currency of AUD10,000 
or more, or the equivalent in foreign currency submitted by reporting entities that provide financial 
and bullion services.
TTR-GS Threshold Transaction Report. A report of a transfer of physical currency or e-currency of AUD10,000 
or more, or the equivalent in foreign currency submitted by reporting entities that provide gambling 
services.
TTR-ISI Threshold Transaction Report. A report of a transfer of physical currency or e-currency of AUD10,000 
or more, or the equivalent in foreign currency submitted by reporting entities that provide 
investment, superannuation and insurance services.
TTR-MSB Threshold Transaction Report. A report of a transfer of physical currency or e-currency of AUD10,000 
or more, or the equivalent in foreign currency submitted by reporting entities that are money services 
businesses
