ICP Form capture macro

Instructions on how to use the ICP Form capture macro.

Last published 26 October 2023

Favourite Notes Collapse all 
Background

This page provides instructions on how to use the ICP Form capture macro. 

Purpose

This tool:

extracts information from multiple tabs (up to 22) in an ICP form, and 

adds it into a single, readable Microsoft Word document, without the need to copy and paste. 

Such functionality is currently not available in ICP.

The following options are also included:

ability to choose to include or remove page/tab titles

ability to choose which tabs to include or remove from the final document

ability to choose not to include blank fields

document formatting option.

Other Microsoft Office macros should not be in operation while the ICP Form capture macro is active. However, other instances of Excel and Word can still be open.

Recent updates

30/05/2023

	

Macro name update.

	

SD-68170

Procedure Steps
Installing the macro
Step
	Action


1

	

Go to the BDA hub
Opens in a new window
 and install the ICP Form capture macro.




2

	

Wait for the installation to finish.

When the installation has finished, the following message will appear:

'ICP Form capture macro has been installed and an icon added to your desktop.'




3

	

Go to your desktop and confirm the shortcut icon has been added to your desktop.

Using the macro
Step
	Action


1

	

Double-click on the shortcut to open the file ICP Form capture macro.

The following warning message may appear: There are 1 existing instance(s) of this BDA running. Select 'OK' to terminate them and launch a new copy of the BDA or select 'Cancel' to abort'.

If this message appears, select OK.




2

	

An ICP Form Capture message will appear asking you to use the Web Version of the form. If there are issues using the Web Version, use the Excel Version.

If you use the:

Web Version, you may be prompted to sign in
Excel Version and a yellow banner appears with the Security Warning 'Application add-ins have been disabled', 
exit the macro
select the Enable Content button
select the Load Macro button.
If you are working on a suspended form in ICP steps 3 to 7 are not necessary.



3

	

Select the Check for Form button to open ICP in Internet Explorer browser.

Only one session of ICP will be used if there are multiple sessions open. The latest session opened will be used by the macro to capture form information.



4

	

Complete the following:

enter relevant taxpayer details in ICP
select the taxpayer 
go to the relevant form.

5	

Complete the following:

open the first page of the ICP form you wish to capture in the View Form screen
go to the macro form.

6	

Select the Check for Form button again.

Only checked tabs will be included in the document.

The ICP Form Found message will appear at the bottom of the form if the macro has found a valid form to capture.

If you are not in a valid ICP form or have not entered taxpayer details, the macro will display an error message at the bottom of the form. Possible error messages are:

'No taxpayer details found in ICP. You need to input a taxpayer's TFN into ICP first.'

'You are not on a valid form page in ICP'.

Return to ICP and repeat the search for the valid form.


7	

Complete the following:

tick the checkboxes to select tabs required in the final Word document
select the appropriate other document options from the bottom right-hand corner of the form.

8	

Select the Capture Form button and wait for it to copy and paste into Microsoft Word.

This may take a few minutes depending on the number of tabs and information being captured.

Once the capture has completed, the form will display a Finished message.

An unsaved Microsoft Word document with the captured information will open. Responsibility rests with the user to check taxpayer details in the macro form to ensure that the macro has captured information from the correct ICP session.

9	

Complete the following:

save or attach the word document as required
select Exit to close the Capture window
To capture further forms, repeat steps 4 to 8.
close the Excel spreadsheet if no more forms need to be captured
select the No button for saving 
changes to the macro spreadsheet, and
clipboard information.
