Note: Do not request a sundry debit posting for overpayments for tax periods starting after 31 May 2014 refer to Division 142 of A New Tax System (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999.

This referral is to be used when you revise an activity statement to zero that was originally lodged with a positive net amount (that is, the BAS is payable) and the taxpayer has paid that amount. A credit amount will remain on the running balance account (RBA) equal to what the taxpayer originally overpaid. Where Section 105-65 of the Tax Administration Act 1953 applies to restrict the amount that has been overpaid, to prevent the overpaid amount from being refunded a sundry debit entry (in the amount of the overpayment) will need to be made.

You should not make a referral for a sundry debit posting to a taxpayer's account for the purposes of Section 105-65 until:

any requests by the taxpayer for a refund of overpaid GST have been referred to TAPP/Indirect Tax Client Advice for a decision on the application of section 105-65 and you have been advised that Section 105-65 applies.
