Return types

The 2 return types are ORG (original) and REV (revision), and it cannot be changed. IPS defaults to the type of activity statement required, depending on the action nominated for the activity statement selected from the Activity statement list screen.

These return types are relevant to both the taxpayer and the ATO as follows:

the taxpayer lodges their original activity statement (ORG) and may revise the activity statement (REV)
the ATO can make an original assessment where the taxpayer has not lodged the activity statement (ORG) and may revise an activity statement lodged by the taxpayer (REV).
Assessment types

The 2 types of assessments that can be made when processing activity statements (net amount and/or net fuel amount) are ATO or SLF.

ATO

Use the assessment type of ATO where the assessment (original or revision) is as a result of your compliance actions.

Examples of when to use ATO are:

You determine that the amount for input tax credits on the activity statement was overstated as a result of an audit. You generate an ATO revision (ATO REV) and include the amended amounts.
The taxpayer has not lodged outstanding activity statements and after unsuccessful attempts to obtain lodgments, you determine the net amounts and make ATO original assessments (ATO ORG) for the tax periods in IPS.
the taxpayer made a voluntary disclosure after being notified of an audit and you determine that the taxpayer's amounts are incorrect. You generate an ATO revision (ATO REV) to amend the amounts. A notice of amended assessment issues.
SLF

Where the taxpayer lodges a voluntary disclosure (SLF REV) via a paper revised activity statement or electronically (for example via online services), it has already been input as a SLF REV in IPS.

Where the taxpayer provides a voluntary disclosure (SLF REV) to you in writing (correspondence), input the amounts as a SLF REV in IPS. This includes where the voluntary disclosure is within or outside the scope of an audit or review. The voluntary disclosure is processed as a SLF whether you have accepted the taxpayer's amounts at face value without any analysis or where your analysis determines that the taxpayer's amounts are correct.

Revisions (SLF and ATO)

There are two types of revisions that can be generated in IPS:

SLF revision - revised amounts provided by a taxpayer, and
ATO revision - revised amounts determined by the ATO (assessment and amended assessment).

All revisions must be processed in IPS.

You must ensure:

all amounts on the original activity statement are transposed to the revised activity statement. Where they are not, refer to original amounts did not carry forward

the correct assessment type (SLF or ATO) is used when processing a revision, and

that notes are added against each activity statement actioned in IPS and the correct revision process is applied to your case.

