Raising ATO originals

An ATO original assessment is made when an entity has not lodged an activity statement, and you determine the entity's amounts (for example net amount).

SLF ORG issued to taxpayer

You must ensure that the original activity statement (Type: 'ORG' Assmt: 'SLF') for the relevant period has issued to the taxpayer, that is, the taxpayer has been provided with an opportunity to lodge the activity statement, before raising an ATO original (view the 'Activity Statement List' screen in IPS for an activity statement (SLF ORG) for the relevant tax period with a status of 'GEN' (generated) or 'DES' (despatched)).

You must ensure that you generate an activity statement with the Type: 'ORG' and Assmt: 'SLF' and issue the activity statement to the taxpayer where you:

determine that a taxpayer was not registered for a period but was required to be registered
update the registration details for the entity backdating or reinstating registration, and
this action results in periods where no activity statement has issued to the taxpayer.

Importantly, this should be completed immediately after the registration update occurs. This will ensure that the taxpayer is provided with ample opportunity to lodge the activity statement prior to you having to make any decision regarding an original assessment.

