Notices of assessment/amended assessment

When the Commissioner makes an assessment/amended assessment of the net amount (GST, WET, LCT amounts) and/or net fuel amount (FTC amounts), a notice of assessment/amended assessment must issue to the taxpayer. The notice is conclusive evidence that an assessment/amended assessment has been made.

When processing ATO revisions or ATO original assessments you must ensure the relevant notice issues.

Where amounts at labels W1/W2 are revised, the Commissioner is not making an amended assessment of these amounts and so a notice of amended assessment does not issue nor does a letter issue from IPS. Instead, you are required to provide an explanation of the changes to these labels in the Reasons for decision to the taxpayer.

