Correcting IPS keying errors

You may make an IPS keying error as part of conducting a compliance activity.

Note: the 2 scenarios outlined below assume that the ASAPS amounts, decisions and outcomes and the finalisation letter are all correct and that an error has occurred only in inputting the amounts or assessment codes into IPS.

Incorrect amounts input in IPS and activity statement is in finalised status

The automated notice is viewable in the CCH in Siebel the day before it issues. This is too late to cancel the notice prior to it issuing if it is incorrect. The notice cannot be cancelled.

Where you identify that an incorrect amount was input in IPS, you should not cancel the ATO revision or the notice. Instead, process another ATO revision in IPS to reflect the correct amount.

You only have a limited timeframe to input the correct amounts before the notice is generated and issued.

if you identify the error prior to 6:00 pm (AEST) on the day you input the amounts in IPS (day 1), process another ATO revision in IPS to reflect the correct amounts. The notice will include both ATO revisions.
if you identify the error after 6:00 pm (AEST) on the day you input the amounts in IPS (day 1) or on day 2, process another ATO revision in IPS to reflect the correct amounts. Two separate notices will issue - one notice will include the first ATO revision and the other notice will include the subsequent ATO revision.

Example:

The taxpayer reported the following amounts on their activity statement: 1A $50,000 and 1B $30,000 (net amount of $20,000 DR).
As a result of compliance action, label 1B was decreased to $20,000 (net amount of $30,000 DR) in IPS.
Prior to 6:00 pm on the day that the amounts were input in IPS, you identified that the label 1B amount of $20,000 was incorrect. The correct label 1B amount is $18,000 (net amount of $32,000 DR) and you input this amount in IPS.
One notice of amended assessment will issue reflecting the 2 ATO revisions; the first ATO revision where the net amount increased from $20,000 DR to $30,000 DR and the second revision where the net amount increased from $30,000 DR to $32,000 DR. So, the net amount increased by $12,000 (from $20,000 DR to $32,000 DR).
For this same example but on day 2 you identified that the incorrect label 1B amount was input. You input the correct amount of $18,000 on this day. Two notices of amended assessment will issue. The first notice will include the first ATO revision where the net amount increased from $20,000 DR to $30 ,00 DR; the second notice will include the second ATO revision where the net amount increased from $30,000 DR to $32,000 DR. 

Where you identify that an incorrect amount was input in IPS after the notice issued to the taxpayer:

Contact the taxpayer and advise that a keying error was made and another notice of amended assessment will issue. The first notice is still valid.
Process another ATO revision in IPS to reflect the correct amounts. An automated notice of amended assessment will issue. 

Incorrect assessment code input into IPS resulting in a default assessment being keyed as a SLF ORIGINAL instead of an ATO ORIGINAL

Where the taxpayer has not lodged outstanding activity statements and you assess the net amount/net fuel amount, an ATO original (ATO ORG) rather than a self-original (SLF ORG) should be processed in IPS.

Where you incorrectly input the amounts as a SLF ORG, a revision cannot be made to correct the error and the only option is to cancel the self-original.

Case officers generally do not have access to cancel activity statements once they are keyed and are in finalised status in IPS and must make a referral to Activity Statement Exceptions (ASE).  

Request and await confirmation of the cancellation of the SLF ORIGINAL by ASE following the instructions in the IT, GST and Excise Referrals and Escalations Guide. For urgent assistance, phone 1300 130 926 or x92144.

Do not proceed to the next step until ASE advise that the assessment has been cancelled.


Update ASAPS ensuring the correct assessment code of ATO ORG is shown on the IPS keying guide, if necessary.
Process an ATO ORIGINAL in IPS using the ASAPS IPS keying guide.
A system generated notice of assessment will issue with a new issue date. A system generated notice would not have issued when the SLF ORIGINAL was processed.
Prepare a covering letter (a letter template in eLetters is not available) which explains that a new automated notice will issue.
What you need to do
 

Cancellations of activity statements can only occur in very limited circumstances and both the access to the cancellation function and permission to use this functionality within IPS is limited.

The reasons for cancellation are outlined in the IPS Help Manual
Opens in a new window
 under the heading 'HOW DO I CANCEL AN ACTIVITY STATEMENT, ANNUAL GST RETURN, OR ANNUAL GST INFORMATION REPORT?'

Very rarely will you be able to request cancellation of an activity statement. Instead, ASE cancel activity statements.

Manual notices

Where it is necessary to personally serve a manual notice to the client (for example covert operations) or there are system issues that prevent issuing an automated notice (for example automated notices cannot issue to a limited registration entity (LRE)):

suppress the automated notice by answering No to the question in IPS 'Do you require the system to generate a notice of assessment?'

prepare and issue a manual notice. Refer to Issuing a manual notice approved practice
