Activity Statement Amendment and Penalty System (ASAPS) guide
ASAPS (Activity Statement Amendment and Penalty System)

Support in undertaking amendments, assessments of activity statement tax related liabilities and administrative penalty

Last published 18 October 2023

Favourite Notes 

The Activity Statement Amendment and Penalty System (ASAPS) supports case officers undertaking amendments and/or assessments of activity statement tax related liabilities and associated administrative penalty decisions.

ASAPS is owned, managed and supported by GST Registry Integrity and Systems Support
Opens in a new window
.



About ASAPS

ASAPS obtains activity statement data in real time or from the Enterprise Data Warehouse. This data is then used to input amendment and/or assessment and penalty decision information. A series of outputs can be generated for inclusion in reports and client correspondence, including:

summary of activity statement amendments and/or assessments tables
summary of penalty decision tables
an Instalment Processing System (IPS) keying guide
a Corporate Penalty System (CPS) keying guide, and
a pre-populated GIC/SIC Calculator.

Manual assessment and penalty notices are no longer generated using ASAPS due to the ADD bypass project and the ASFP release.

User guide

The ASAPS user guide
Opens in a new window
 (accessed from the GST Program Systems Library) contains important information on the use of the system and when it must be used.

 

Approved 'retained system'

ASAPS was developed in 2013 and endorsed as an approved 'retained system' for correspondence by the Enterprise Correspondence Forum on 12 June 2014 and complies with CEI 2014/01/07
Opens in a new window
.

 

